Author: Marius Momeu <marius.momeu@berkeley.edu>
Date:   Sun Nov 15 01:21:52 2026 +0000

    ubc_check.c: wrap 1 item (wave-221/batch-0/run-1)

    st::dv_info_t

    The module's one type, wrapped ahead of its port batch, since sha1.c's
    C reads its layout from sha1_dvs: DvInfo, a define_ctype! layout with
    DvInfoRef and DvInfoMut, plain data, Copy, Send and Sync, so that the
    port's table can be a static. DvInfo::new is a const fn refusing a
    recompression step outside 0..80, a mask bit outside 0..32 (which
    sha1_process uses unchecked as an index and a shift) and a mask word
    other than 0; getters for the four fields sha1.c reads (dvType, testt,
    maskb, dm). The raw bindings allowlist dv_info_t (wrapper.h gains
    ubc_check.h); the analysis is submitted to the ownership store. Seven
    unit_pub, two ub_safe and two compile-fail tests. The package verified
    alone in bundled mode; package-gate-procedure gains this run's
    occurrence and the command that verified.

    Co-Authored-By: crustify <crustify@berkeley.edu>

